  "label": "User projected onto the textual material overlaying the images",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'two sad images from american history' which frames both visual elements as part of 'American history'. This text acts as a deictic label that imposes a specific historical and emotional context onto the viewer's perception of both images, even though the bottom image is from a French publication and depicts a non-American event. The user is thus projected onto this textual material, which dictates the interpretive framework for the entire meme.",
